- B | go for it openly against the other candidate, and win the panel over first | v: power, achievement | mark: made an enemy | title: senior nurse or midwife | tribal: put yourself forward openly against the other hearth's healer, and win the elders over first | magic: put your name forward against the sisters' candidate, and win the steward over first | chance: 40
- R | tell the panel bluntly what the ward lacks, and how you would fight for it | v: self-direction, benevolence | title: senior nurse or midwife | tribal: tell the women bluntly at the fire what the band's births lack, and how you would mend it | magic: tell the council bluntly what the ward lacks, and how you would fight for it | chance: 40
- G | go for it as the one who has known the ward and its families longest | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: stayed home | identity | title: senior nurse or midwife | tribal: put yourself forward as the one who has known every hearth's births longest | magic: put your name forward as the one who has known the ward and its families longest | chance: 40
- BG | ask to act up in the post for six months, and prove it first | v: achievement, security | self_control: + | tribal: ask to keep the births beside the old birth-keeper for a season first, and prove it | magic: ask to keep the ward as acting matron for six months, and prove it first | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 82
- UB | go for a specialist's post instead, with better hours and better pay | v: achievement, self-direction | self_control: - | tribal: become the band's keeper of the strong plants instead, and leave the births to another | magic: seek a place at the apothecaries' bench instead, with its better hours and better pay | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 82
- UR | turn the post down in writing until the ward gets the two nurses it lacks | v: universalism, self-direction | mark: defied an authority | closed: approval: a post refused on conditions; backfire: the managers give the post to someone else, and remember the letter | tribal: refuse to keep the births until the elders give the sick a second healer | magic: refuse the post in writing until the council gives the ward the two sisters it lacks | chance: 82
- WG | put your colleague's name forward, and offer to stand beside them | v: benevolence, tradition | binds | mark: made a friend | tribal: speak at the fire for the healer of your own hearth, and offer to stand beside them | magic: speak to the council for the sister at your side, and offer to stand beside her | chance: 82
- WR | ask the whole team at handover who they would want in charge | v: conformity, benevolence | tribal: ask the women of the band at the fire who they would want to keep the births | magic: ask the sisters of the ward at the change of watch who they would want as matron | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 82
works: Within the month it is settled, and the ward turns to {N} first.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the ward is in good hands, and {N} sleeps well that month.
fails: The post goes to {rival}, and {N} has to smile all through the leaving party for {mentor}.
fails: It goes badly at the one moment that mattered, and the post goes to someone from outside.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6. patients come from far away (pairs D5b)
# The summit, a facet on the healing career held (senior nurse or midwife, nurse, midwife, physician or complementary
# therapist of eight years or more; LIFE_CALLINGS adds the exact years): families travel from far away to be in {N}'s
# care. Every colour's way of taking the name on is a try at the brief's real chance of a healer known across the land
# (6): `title: renowned healer` with `grants: families who send for you`. A step at real odds, not a long shot, so no perk
# on failure, and no mark on the singles (the title and the bond are their two footprints). The pairs at 80 are the
# honest other ways: part-time on the ward and a rented room for the far families, a weekend a month on the road, two
# young nurses taught, a clinic day asked of the managers, and a careful letter to each family about care near home.
# Every colour's mean is 43.

== patients come from far away
tier: life event
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-100
holds: senior nurse or midwife | midwife | nurse | physician | complementary therapist
tenure: 8-100
per_year: 0 0 0 .01 .03 .02
drivers: community+.3 fortune+.2
times: per senior nurse or midwife, nurse, midwife, physician or complementary therapist of eight years or more a year: about 1 in 60 find patients travelling from other towns, by word of mouth, to be in their care (estimate); about 5 lives in 100,000 become healers known across the country (catalogue share; estimate)
likelier: years with the same district's families, a way of caring of one's own, a story in the papers, a mentor who sends patients on
rarer: a busy city practice where nobody knows anyone's name, a move away, a hard year on the ward
gap: 5-15
domain: career.5
tone: joy
life: work, meaning
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague, mentor, friend
earth: families from other towns begin to ask for the healer by name, and the waiting list grows longer than the district's own
tribal: families from far bands send runners for the healer by name, and some walk for days to camp beside the healer's fire
magic: families from distant towns of the realm write and travel to be in the healer's hands, and the temple house's door is never quiet
scene: It began with one family, then another, then a woman who drove four hours with her father because a neighbour had said {Ns} name. Now letters come every week, the waiting list runs to the spring, and a reporter from a big paper has asked to spend a day on the rounds. {boss} wants to know what {N} means to do about it.
scene W: People come because the care is good, and the care is good because it is done right, every time. {N} would like to keep it that way, however many come.
scene U: {N} has wondered for years why some ways of caring work better than others. Now there are enough patients to find out.
scene B: A name like this opens doors: a post of one's own making, a book, a seat at the tables where the money is decided. {N} knows it will not last forever.
scene R: The families who come so far are frightened and hopeful at once. {N} feels every one of them, and wants to say yes to them all.
scene G: {N} never set out to be known. The work grew the way a garden does, one season on another, and now people come from far away to sit in it.
scene tribal: Runners have come from bands three valleys away, asking for {N} by name, and two families have walked for days to camp beside the healer's fire with their sick. The traders carry the story from camp to camp, and {boss}, the eldest of the band, asks what {N} means to do about it.
scene magic: Letters come under the seals of distant towns, and families travel for days to sit in the temple house's long hall and wait for {N}. A broadsheet writer from the capital has asked to follow the rounds, and {boss}, the temple's steward, wants to know what {N} means to do.
- W | open a fair list for the far patients, first come first seen, and keep to it | v: universalism, conformity | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | tribal: take the far sick in the order they came, by the old rule, and keep to it | magic: open a fair roll for the far patients, first come first seen, and keep to it | chance: 6
- U | study what works in your care, and publish it so others can do the same | v: achievement, universalism | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | habit | tribal: watch what works in your care season on season, and teach it to every band's healers | magic: study what works in your care, and set it down in a book for other healers | chance: 6
- B | let the reporter follow the rounds, and put your name to your way of caring | v: power, achievement | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | identity | tribal: let the traders carry your name from camp to camp, and name your way of healing for yourself | magic: let the broadsheet writer follow the rounds, and put your name to your way of caring | chance: 6
- R | say yes to every family that comes, and work the evenings to see them all | v: benevolence, stimulation | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | self_control: - | tribal: say yes to every family that comes, and tend them by firelight after the day's work | magic: say yes to every family that comes, and work the evenings to see them all | chance: 6
- G | keep the district's own families first, and let the far ones wait their turn | v: tradition, benevolence | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | tribal: keep your own band's families first, and let the far ones wait their turn | magic: keep the lower town's own families first, and let the far ones wait their turn | chance: 6
- BR | go part-time on the ward, and see the far families in a rented room | v: self-direction, achievement | habit | tribal: leave the band's daily tending to others, and see the far families in a shelter of your own | magic: give up half your watches, and see the far families in a hired room in the town | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 80
- RG | go out to the far families yourself, one weekend a month | v: benevolence, stimulation | body: light | tribal: walk out to the far bands yourself, one moon in every three | magic: ride out to the far families yourself, one week in every month | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 80
- UG | take two young nurses under your wing, and teach them all you know | v: benevolence, achievement | grants: apprentice of one's own | binds | tribal: take two young healers of the band beside you, and teach them all you know | magic: take two young sisters under your wing, and teach them all you know | chance: 80
- WB | ask the managers for a clinic day of your own for the far patients | v: achievement, security | tribal: ask the elders for a shelter by the camp where the far sick may wait | magic: ask the council for a day in the week of your own for the far patients | foot: place care.houses | chance: 80
- WU | write each far family a careful letter on what can be done near home | v: universalism, benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | tribal: send each far family's runner home with a careful word on what their own healers can do | magic: write each far family a careful letter on what their own healers can do | chance: 80
works: By the end of the year {Ns} name is known far beyond the district, and the families keep coming.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the far families are helped, and the district's own still come first.
fails: The fuss dies down after a season, and the waiting list shrinks back to the district's own.
fails: The far families find another healer to talk about, and {N} goes back to the ordinary weeks, a little relieved.

# ================================================================ fall and wrong

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7. the wrong dose on the night shift (triads D3a)
# A dose mistake caught in time: the patient is fine by morning, and nobody else knows yet. Tell or hide. The wrong sits
# on the UBG triad (Blue's quiet correction of the chart, Black's career kept clean, Green's belief that the body has
# mended and the matter can rest): the chart corrected and nothing said (hid a wrong; closed: approval: a mistake
# hidden; when it fails, the record shows it and `takes_if_fails: licence to prescribe`, the brief's backfire). The
# others: the doctor told and the form filled in, the error traced, the union rep rung first, the patient's daughter
# told face to face, a night at the bedside, the whole of it told to the patient and the ward (owned up), a report that
# changes the drug round, the blame taken alone for a worn-out colleague, fewer night shifts asked. Chances are set by
# act and the singles solved around the triads until every colour's mean is 70.

== the wrong dose on the night shift
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 21-75
holds: senior nurse or midwife | nurse | midwife | physician
per_year: 0 0 .02 .02 .015 .005
drivers: stress+.2 trouble+.1
times: per nurse, midwife, senior nurse or physician a year: about 1 in 50 make a dose mistake that is caught before it does harm (estimate); mistakes with medicines are among the incidents hospitals report most, and most of them harm nobody (patient-safety reporting; estimate); about 3 lives in 100 are nurses (catalogue share)
likelier: long shifts and short staff, two strengths of one medicine kept side by side, a new ward, nights
rarer: a second check on every strong dose, a rested team, a ward with time to stop and look
gap: 5-15
domain: career.5
tone: trouble
life: work, health
horizon: week
roles: colleague, boss, mentor
earth: at four in the morning a dose mistake comes to light: a patient given twice the dose, now watched and safe, and fine by morning
tribal: before dawn in the sickness shelter the healer finds that a sick man was given twice the measure of the strong root, and that he will wake well
magic: before dawn the healer finds in the ward book that an old carter was given a double draught of the sleeping medicine, and that he will wake well
scene: At four in the morning, checking the charts, {N} sees it: the old man in bed twelve was given twice his dose of a strong painkiller at midnight. {colleague}, at the end of a fourteen-hour day, drew it up, and {N} checked it and signed. He is breathing easily and his colour is good; the doctor will say he needs watching and nothing more, and by morning he will be fine. Nobody else has noticed yet.
scene W: There is a form for this, and a reason for the form. {N} knows the rule: report it at once, whatever it costs.
scene U: Two strengths of the same medicine, kept side by side in boxes that look almost alike. {N} can already see how it happened, and how it will happen again.
scene B: A mistake on the record stays on the record. {N} thinks of the promotion list, the registration board, and the managers who will want a name to blame.
scene R: {Ns} stomach turns over. The man in bed twelve tells jokes about his grandchildren, and {N} could have hurt him.
scene G: He is asleep, and his breathing is slow and even. The body has its own ways of mending, and {N} can sit beside it and watch it mend.
scene tribal: In the sickness shelter before dawn, {N} counts the roots left in the healer's bag and sees it: the old hunter with the cough was given twice the measure of the strong root at nightfall, from {colleague}'s mixing and {Ns} own hand. He sleeps deeply and breathes well, and by morning he will wake, but nobody else knows yet.
scene magic: Checking the ward book before dawn, {N} sees that the old carter in the end bed was given a double draught of the sleeping medicine at midnight, mixed by {colleague} at the end of a long watch and given by {N}. He breathes easily and will wake well, but nobody else has noticed.
- W | tell the night doctor at once, and fill in the incident form before handover | v: conformity, security | identity | mark: owned up | tribal: wake the old healer at once, and tell the elders at first light, as the custom is | magic: wake the night physician at once, and write it in the ward book before the change of watch | chance: 69
- U | work out exactly how the two doses were mixed up, step by step | v: achievement, universalism | mark: learned a skill | tribal: work out exactly how the two measures of root were mixed up, step by step | magic: work out exactly how the two draughts were mixed up, step by step | chance: 71
- B | ring the union rep before saying a word to anyone | v: security, power | self_control: + | tribal: go first to the old healer who has the elders' ear, before saying a word to anyone | magic: go first to the sisters' advocate in the temple, before saying a word to anyone | foot: person go-between | chance: 70
- R | tell the patient's daughter yourself, face to face, first thing in the morning | v: benevolence, self-direction | mark: owned up | tribal: tell the old hunter's daughter yourself, face to face, at first light | magic: tell the carter's daughter yourself, face to face, first thing in the morning | chance: 67
- G | sit by the patient until morning, watching every breath until it passes | v: benevolence | body: light | tribal: sit by the old hunter until morning, watching every breath until it passes | magic: sit by the old carter until morning, watching every breath until it passes | foot: lesson stay close when it matters | chance: 72
- WUR | tell the patient and the ward the whole of it, and write it all down | v: conformity, benevolence | self_control: + | mark: owned up | identity | tribal: tell the old hunter and the whole band the whole of it at the fire | magic: tell the carter and the whole ward the whole of it, and write it all in the book | chance: 75
- WUB | report it to the safety team with a plan for a second check on strong doses | v: universalism, security | tribal: ask the elders that every measure of the strong root be checked by a second healer | magic: ask the council that every strong draught be checked by a second sister | foot: lesson tired hands need a second check | chance: 72
- WRG | put your name alone on the report, to shield the worn-out colleague | v: benevolence | tribal: tell the elders it was your hand alone, to shield the worn-out healer who mixed it | magic: write your name alone in the book, to shield the worn-out sister who mixed it | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 66
- UBG | correct the chart quietly, say nothing, and watch the patient yourself till morning | v: security, power | mark: hid a wrong | self_control: - | takes_if_fails: licence to prescribe | closed: approval: a mistake hidden; backfire: the pharmacy count and the record show it, and the leave to give strong medicines is taken away | tribal: say nothing, put back a root from your own store, and watch the old hunter yourself till morning | magic: mend the ward book quietly, say nothing, and watch the carter yourself till morning | chance: 60
- BRG | ask the manager for fewer night shifts, before tiredness does it again | v: security, self-direction | tribal: ask the elders to let you rest from the night tending, before tiredness does it again | magic: ask the steward for fewer night watches, before tiredness does it again | foot: means health+.04 | chance: 78
works: The patient wakes well and hungry, and the matter is settled the way {N} chose.
works: A month later the ward does things a little differently, and {N} can look the patient's family in the eye.
fails: The patient is fine by morning, but the matter goes badly: questions, meetings and a cold silence among the others.
fails: Word gets out the wrong way, and for a season {N} is the name the others whisper about.

# ================================================================ long shot

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8. the remedy that worked (triads D5b)
# A way of caring the families talk about: a dressing of honey and garden marigold, made the way {grandparent} made it,
# heals the old wounds that would not close. It comes to a nurse, midwife or complementary therapist of three years or
# more, or a senior nurse or midwife, from thirty, the title's first age (`tenure: 3-99`; LIFE_CALLINGS_LONGSHOTS has
# the exact years). The long shot is the summit at 3 in every colour, `title: renowned healer`, the facet on the career each
# holder has, with `grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed` (core/longshot.py), so every single fits everyone who meets
# the moment. The triads at 84, the brief's ways to weigh it: teach it, write it up, a day a week for the wounds nobody
# else can heal, keep using it on the ward without leave (a closed: approval act), or keep it for the families. Every
# colour's mean is 43.5.

== the remedy that worked
tier: life event
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-95
holds: nurse | midwife | complementary therapist | senior nurse or midwife
tenure: 3-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .01 .01 .01
drivers: community+.2 fortune+.3
times: per nurse, midwife, complementary therapist or senior nurse of three years or more a year: about 1 in 100 find a way of caring of their own that the families start to talk about (estimate); honey and plant dressings for slow wounds are old remedies that ward studies have looked at again (estimate); about 5 lives in 100,000 become healers known across the country (catalogue share)
likelier: years with the same families, a garden or an old family way, a mentor who listens, a year when the papers want a good story
rarer: a ward that changes its dressings by the book alone, no time to watch a wound for weeks, a move away
gap: 6-15
domain: career.5
tone: joy
life: work, meaning, nature
horizon: months
roles: grandparent, colleague, mentor, boss
earth: a dressing of honey and garden marigold heals the old wounds that would not close, and the families start to talk about it
tribal: a poultice of wild honey and the yellow meadow flower closes the old wounds that would not heal, and the bands start to talk about it
magic: a salve of honey and marigold from the healer's own garden closes the wounds the temple's physicians gave up on, and the town talks of nothing else
scene: The old farmer from the next village had a wound on his leg that had not closed in a year. {N} tried a dressing of honey and marigold from {Ns} own garden, the way {grandparent} used to make it, and in six weeks it had healed. Then a second wound healed, and a third. Now the families ask for {N} by name, the local paper has rung, and {mentor} says it ought to be written up properly.
scene W: If it works, it should be done properly: measured, written down, checked, and taught the same way every time. {N} has the notes of every dressing in a folder.
scene U: Why does it work? {N} has read everything there is on honey and wounds, and there is a question in it nobody seems to have asked.
scene B: Something like this could make a name. {N} thinks of the conferences, the books, and the people who would want to put their own name to it first.
scene R: {N} cannot stop thinking about all the people out there with wounds that will not close, waiting and hoping. Every one of them should have this.
scene G: The marigolds came from {grandparent}'s seed, saved year after year. The garden gives, and the body heals, if both are given time.
scene tribal: The old hunter of the next band had a wound on his leg that had not closed since the summer. {N} laid on a poultice of wild honey and the yellow meadow flower, the way {grandparent} did it, and before the moon was out it had healed. Now runners come from far camps asking for the healer who knows the yellow flower, and the traders carry the story from fire to fire.
scene magic: The temple's physicians had given up on the old carter's leg, and {N} dressed it with a salve of honey and marigold from {Ns} own garden, the way {grandparent} made it. In six weeks it had healed. Now families queue at the temple house door, a printer wants to sell the recipe, and the masters of the apothecaries' college have written to ask what is in it.
- W | write it up as a careful protocol, and send it to the national nursing college | v: conformity, universalism | title: renowned healer | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | self_control: + | tribal: set it down as the band's own way, step by step, and teach it at the great gathering | magic: write it up as a careful rule of practice, and send it to the apothecaries' college | chance: 3
- U | run a proper trial with a doctor on twenty patients, and publish the results | v: achievement, universalism | title: renowned healer | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | tribal: try it on every slow wound in three bands, season by season, and mark which ones close | magic: try it with a temple physician on twenty patients, and set the results in a book | chance: 3
- B | give the dressing your own name, and take it to every conference that will listen | v: power, achievement | title: renowned healer | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | tribal: give the poultice your own name, and carry it to every band's gathering | magic: give the salve your own name, and show it before every guild that will listen | chance: 3
- R | say yes to every family who writes, and go to them, however far | v: benevolence, stimulation | door | title: renowned healer | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | body: light | tribal: say yes to every runner who comes, and walk to the far bands, however far | magic: say yes to every family who writes, and ride out to them, however far | chance: 3
- G | grow the marigolds in your own garden, and teach the families to make it | v: tradition, benevolence | title: renowned healer | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | habit | tribal: gather the yellow flower in the meadows each summer, and teach every hearth to make it | magic: grow the marigolds in your own garden, and teach the town's families to make it | foot: place prod.land | chance: 3
- WUG | teach it to the young nurses on the ward, one patient at a time | v: benevolence, tradition | grants: apprentice of one's own | tribal: teach it to the young healers of the band, one wound at a time | magic: teach it to the young sisters of the ward, one patient at a time | chance: 84
- WUB | write it up for the hospital's own bulletin, with the dates and the weeks | v: achievement, conformity | tribal: tell it at the elders' fire, wound by wound and moon by moon, so it is remembered | magic: write it up for the temple house's own book, with the dates and the weeks | foot: lesson write down what works | chance: 84
- WBR | ask the managers for one day a week for the wounds that will not heal | v: achievement, benevolence | habit | tribal: ask the elders to free you from the hunt one day in four, for the wounds that will not heal | magic: ask the council for one day a week for the wounds that will not heal | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 84
- URG | keep using it on the ward's old wounds, without waiting for the managers' leave | v: self-direction, benevolence | mark: defied an authority | closed: approval: a dressing used on the ward without leave; backfire: the medicines committee hears of it, and the senior nurse is told to stop and write it up | tribal: keep laying it on every slow wound, without waiting for the elders' word | magic: keep using it on the ward's old wounds, without waiting for the physicians' leave | chance: 84
- BRG | keep it for the district's families, and turn the reporter from the paper away | v: security, tradition | tribal: keep it for your own band's families, and send the far runners away | magic: keep it for the lower town's families, and turn the printer away | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 84
works: Within the year {Ns} dressing is talked about far beyond the district, and the wounds go on closing.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the families keep coming, and the wounds that would not heal begin to close.
fails: The fuss fades after a season, the talk moves on, and {N} goes back to the ordinary dressings and the ordinary weeks.
fails: The next three wounds heal no faster than any others, and people stop asking, though {N} keeps making it.

# ================================================================ world-only (tribal)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. the sickness in the winter camp (only: tribal; triads D6b)
# The tribal world's crossing to the summit (callings/worlds.py, WORLD_ONLY_CALLINGS): a fever runs through the winter
# camp, and the healer who brings the camp through becomes the healer every band sends for. Each one-colour way of
# nursing it is a try at the brief's real chance, 6: `title: renowned healer` (the facet on the healing career held) with
# `grants: families who send for you`. The gate (LIFE_CALLINGS) lets in the band's birth-keeper ([senior nurse or
# midwife]) and its nurses and midwives of two winters, from thirty, the title's first age (a [care worker] has no
# career the facet sits on). The
# triads at 70, the honest other ways: every hearth taught to boil its water, the camp moved upriver, the shaman asked
# to call on the river spirit (the one supernatural act: the magic is the spirit's, never the healer's own; closed:
# approval: the spirit's price, with a backfire), the next band's healer bought with furs, and the worst of the sick
# nursed apart. Nobody dies in the text: the fever passes and the camp recovers. Every colour's mean is 38.

== the sickness in the winter camp
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
holds: senior nurse or midwife | nurse | midwife
tenure: 2-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .02 .02
drivers: harsh+.2 community+.1
times: per healer of the band in the tribal world (the birth-keeper, or a nurse or midwife of two winters) a year: about 1 in 50, in a winter when a fever runs through the camp (estimate); small bands living close in winter shelters met fevers most winters, and most passed (estimate)
likelier: a hard winter in one camp, a slow pool for drinking water, a band crowded with visitors from the gathering
rarer: a mild winter on the move, clean running water, a band kept apart from the others
gap: 5-10
tone: mixed
life: work, community, health
horizon: months
roles: elder, colleague, rival
tribal: a fever runs through the winter camp by the frozen river, and the band looks to its healer
scene tribal: In the deep of the winter a fever runs through the camp by the frozen river. A dozen of the band lie hot and shivering in their shelters, old hunters and grown men and women alike, and {colleague}, the band's other healer, is down with it too. The elders look to {N}, and the runners from the next band say their healer cannot come before the moon turns.
scene tribal W: The old rule is clear: the sick sleep apart from the well, and the healer goes to each in turn. {N} has seen what happens when nobody keeps it.
scene tribal U: The fever started in the shelters nearest the slow pool below the camp, and nowhere else. {N} keeps thinking about the water.
scene tribal B: Whoever brings the camp through this winter will be spoken of at every fire in the valley. {N} knows it, and so does {rival}.
scene tribal R: {N} has not slept for two nights and does not mean to. There is always another shelter, another hot forehead, another cup of water to hold.
scene tribal G: Fevers come with the deep cold, as they always have, and most of them pass. The willows by the river still hold what the old ones used, under the snow.
- W | keep the sick apart from the well by the old rule, and tend each in turn | v: conformity, security | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | chance: 6
- U | find the water the fever came with, and move the drinking to the clean spring | v: achievement, universalism | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | chance: 6
- B | send runners to every band for their healers' plants, and lead them all | v: power, achievement | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | chance: 6
- R | go from shelter to shelter day and night, until the last fever breaks | v: benevolence, stimulation | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | body: light | chance: 6
- G | brew the willow bark the old ones used for fevers, and carry it to every shelter | v: tradition, benevolence | title: renowned healer | grants: families who send for you | chance: 6
- WUG | teach every hearth to boil its water and keep its sick warm | v: universalism, benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 70
- WUB | ask the elders to move the camp upriver to clean water, and plan the move | v: security, achievement | binds | foot: lesson clean water keeps sickness away | chance: 70
- WRG | ask the shaman to call on the river spirit for a cure, and promise its price | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: took a wild risk | closed: approval: the spirit's price; backfire: the fever passes, but the spirit's price comes due: the band must leave its best winter ground for three winters, and the elders blame the healer | chance: 70
- UBR | trade the band's best furs to the next band for their healer's help | v: benevolence, power | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 70
- BRG | stay in the sick shelter with the worst of them, and keep the others away | v: benevolence, security | body: light | foot: means health-.05 | chance: 70
works: The fever breaks in the shelters one by one, and by the thaw the whole camp is on its feet.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the sickness passes, and the bands along the river hear whose hands tended it.
fails: The fever runs through the camp for a whole moon before it passes, and everyone is thin and tired by the thaw.
fails: The sickness passes in its own time and everyone recovers, but the band gives another healer the credit.
